From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Wrap __isoc23_strtoul

glibc 2.38+ builds call __isoc23_strtoul for strtoul; box86 had the
strtol, strtoll and strtoull variants but not this one, so the call
failed to resolve and xbcompat hung at the dashboard.
---
--- a/src/wrapped/wrappedlibc_private.h
+++ b/src/wrapped/wrappedlibc_private.h
@@ -1764,6 +1764,7 @@
 GO2(__isoc23_strtoll_l, IFppip, strtoll_l)
 GOW(strtoq, IFppi)  // is that ok?
 GO(strtoul, LFppi)
+GO2(__isoc23_strtoul, LFppi, strtoul)
 GO(__strtoul_internal, LFppii)
 GO(strtoull, UFppi)
 GO2(__isoc23_strtoull, UFppi, strtoull)
